WEBVTT

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.350
The moon doesn't change, 
no matter where you're seeing it.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.500
You're seeing the same moon as I am,

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.530
aren't you, Inaba?

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.070
Of course not, chirp!

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.090
There's an eight-hour time difference 
between England and Japan.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:22.660
9:00 PM in England is 5:00 AM 
in Japan, chirp!

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.550
The Earth's round, chirp.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.080
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.570
<i>Something has changed since 
I started waterfall training.</i>

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.050
<i>I can close my eyes,</i>

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.330
<i>but my mind's eye starts 
seeing different things.</i>

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:45.400
<i>A transparent... bird?</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:48.770
<i>No, a man in black?</i>

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:50.560
<i>This is...</i>

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.920
<b>Sixteenth Haunting 
Look at the Full Moon and Jump</b>

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:38.870
Were you able to see it, too?

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.630
Tonight is the full moon.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:44.050
I see.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.980
The bunny in the moon is 
a worldwide concept.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.220
Probably because both rabbits and the 
moon represent a bountiful harvest.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:57.320
The ancient Chinese claimed 
clams live on the moon.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:02.090
And eventually, it changed to toads,

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.350
and then rabbits.

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:09.070
In China, the rabbits on the 
moon make medicine.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.800
It isn't mochi?

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.100
That's right.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.960
They say the medicine the rabbits
 make grants immortality.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.000
Immortality...

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.920
The moon is associated with 
immortality, as well.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.370
Soma, the Indian god of the moon,

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.350
carries amrita, a medicine 
that makes you immortal.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.490
Princess Kaguya had one, too.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:32.270
The moon waxes and wanes,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.790
so it probably symbolizes death and rebirth.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.390
To the ancients, the moon 
was where the gods lived.

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:45.120
And the people who lived 
there were immortal...

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:50.180
<i>While I eat this delicious breakfast, 
I'm learning things.</i>

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.320
<i>Isn't this place great?</i>

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.120
A package?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.170
Wow! When did this get here?

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.740
Those fish are huge!

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.140
They're so plump!

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.180
They look so good!

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.730
Have to cook 'em with salt... 
That's how the Japanese spend autumn.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.270
Once you're home from school, 
get ready for a moon-viewing party!

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:20.060
We'll make mochi, just like the moon rabbit.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.850
This is mochi rice, then?

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:26.430
Yeah! Azuki beans and mochi 
together, for tsukimi dumplings!

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.490
Dumplings, huh?

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:32.170
Fukase usually does it, but we 
don't know if he'll be back today.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.440
This year, making them will be your job.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.080
I'll do my best!

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.500
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.510
Moon viewing?

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.730
I thought only the neighborhood 
association did that.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.090
That's weird.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.670
Shut up! Don't call it weird!

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.720
I've never done that before...

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.560
Maybe in kindergarten?

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.430
Well, I only have a vague memory

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.890
of making dumplings at my grandpa's house.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:01.280
So, Tashiro, I'm gonna have 
to skip club today.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.530
Okay, you owe me.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.130
Owe you what?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.010
Yummy salmon!

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.720
Shioyaki! And sashimi!

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.460
We've got tataki, too!

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:28.370
Intestines! Ruriruri really 
knows how to cook!

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.480
Gotta get some sake... But which?

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.140
Let's eat!

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.970
Yum!

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:42.400
I'm so glad I was born Japanese!

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.070
This mixed-plate appetizer is good, too!

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:50.910
And after that fatty fish, 
natto soup is so refreshing!

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.920
Asian pears.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.800
It's really fall...

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:00.720
Everyone, I got the okay from the landlord!

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:05.950
Usually, we do our moon 
viewing on the porch.

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:09.680
But this year, we'll do it next to 
the waterfall in the baths.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.020
There?

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.810
We'll invite special guests 
and have a big party!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.890
G-Guests?

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:19.720
Patients from Tsukinoki Hospital.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.870
It gets boring at the hospital.

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.140
That's nice.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:27.810
Um, do you mean... ghosts?

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.740
Don't worry! None of them are too impressive!

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.080
Huh...

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:38.640
<i>Tsukinoki Hospital is where Akine-chan 
works, as part of her training.</i>

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:44.030
<i>It's a yokai hospital for yokai that 
are hurt, physically or spiritually.</i>

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.660
<i>It's old and scary.</i>

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:51.510
<b>Examination Room 2</b>

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.060
<i>Normal people would never usually go there.</i>

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:56.190
<i>Most of those that do are homeless 
or elderly with no relatives.</i>

00:06:57.090 --> 00:07:02.780
<i>And 100% of them meet their 
ends at Tsukinoki Hospital.</i>

00:07:03.910 --> 00:07:07.400
<i>Rumors say, if you enter Tsukinoki,
 you cannot leave alive.</i>

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.030
<i>That means even fewer people go.</i>

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.970
No, we're fine with that...

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:16.280
We mostly serve the inhuman.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.700
But we do our best to take care 
of patients that do come, 24/7.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:25.140
But isn't that hard?

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:31.940
Our staff are all spiritualists 
or not human at all.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:35.300
So we can handle any patient.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:39.100
We can take care of them 
without ever getting tired.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.130
I see.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.060
Elderly who have fallen 
into unfortunate straits,

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:48.600
lost their relatives, lost their home,

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:52.730
and come alone to a hospital of death.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:58.300
But in the end, that's good luck, isn't it?

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:13.030
Ultimately, they all pass 
with smiles on their faces.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:19.100
Some of them realize that 
it isn't a normal hospital.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:23.910
"I don't have much time left,

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.810
so nothing surprises me now.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:32.190
Compared to the awful humans I've met,

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:36.120
everyone here is like the Buddha,"

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:38.210
they say.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.630
Humans are...

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:44.600
No matter how cruel it may seem,

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.740
there are many different 
circumstances in this world.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:54.220
Because they understand that, 
the elderly are okay with it.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.950
Isshiki-san...

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:00.760
It's a state they can only reach 
because they have seen so much

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:05.390
of humanity's weakness, cruelty, and sadness.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:08.700
I'm sure that's part of it...

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:15.700
And we also have this big yard.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.990
And there's a big tree.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.090
We keep dogs and cats at the hospital.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:24.230
On nice days, everyone goes outside.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.880
Everyone looks so happy, too.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:33.270
<i>Humans, and things that aren't 
human, laughing together.</i>

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.430
<i>And souls are saved by spending 
an unhappy life's</i>

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:40.850
<i>last days in peace, huh?</i>

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:44.310
Of course, we have all kinds 
of powerful specialists,

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:48.760
so once they die, their spirits go 
immediately to the next world.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:52.520
We use the bodies for various things, though.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.230
<i>I won't ask any more.</i>

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:02.970
L-Landlord?

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:04.460
His friends.

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:06.870
They're helping Ruriruri.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:10.130
Lots of food needs to be made.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.140
The mochi rice is done steaming!

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:16.710
That's your cue, Yushi-kun!

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.100
Right!

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:21.180
I've never done this before!

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.800
Good luck!

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:25.830
At first, do it softly, 
like you're kneading it.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.240
L-Like this?

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:31.970
<i>I-It's hard on my back...</i>

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:34.940
Okay, now pound it.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:36.870
A-All right.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:43.490
Gotta put your hips into it, Yushi-kun.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:46.450
Like when you carry something 
heavy at your job.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:47.700
Right!

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:50.700
You're off-target, Yushi-kun.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.550
Like this?

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.970
Gotta time it better.

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:04.940
Okay, good work.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.320
Are you all right, Yushi-kun?

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:10.310
Oh, I'm fine.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:13.220
I just figured it out...

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:15.150
Glad to hear it.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.650
There's lots more to do!

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:30.160
I-I'm dying...

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.990
K-Kuri?

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.720
It's so good! What is this?

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:40.000
Ankoro mochi.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:41.880
Perfect for moon viewing.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:44.060
What's that?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.250
Salmon and mushroom noppe stew.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:49.800
It has lots of taros, too!

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:53.830
During moon viewings, taro was also eaten.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:57.470
You eat things that are white 
and round, like the moon.

00:11:58.130 --> 00:12:01.430
And so, dumplings replaced taros.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:09.410
Now, go take a bath with Kuri-tan, 
and wash off that exhaustion.

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.700
If Mommy falls asleep, wake him up.

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:15.530
I'm not his mommy!

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:16.880
Hey, where's Daddy?

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:20.810
He's in Europe, on a school trip.

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:23.290
Wait! He isn't Daddy!

00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:26.140
I see... What a shame.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.520
I wanted to look at the moon with him.

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:30.200
Yeah.

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:33.920
I'm sure he'll say he'd have 
rather been here.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.910
I smell food!

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:59.340
I'm back...

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:03.510
Furuhonya-san, you stink.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:08.170
I was in India, on a sudden business trip...

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:10.510
Gimme food.

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.270
Perfect timing.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.430
We're having a moon-viewing party.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:16.430
Yay! Lucky me!

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.560
Take a bath first...

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:22.860
I don't have the energy.

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:26.150
Then, Yushi-kun, give him a bath.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:30.770
<i>I can get my revenge!</i>

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.120
Leave it to me!

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.990
I'll take care of it!

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.120
I'm so happy... Wash me all over.

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:46.040
You smell a little like
red bean paste, Yushi-kun.

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.580
I-It hurts! You stink!

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.800
Where were you, and what were you doing?

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:56.230
<i>I was a fool to think I could 
win, even for a moment.</i>

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:58.760
I feel so much better...

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:02.570
Would you look at that?

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:17.640
Wow!

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:18.840
Way to go, landlord.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.500
It's perfect.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.020
I made it!

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:23.770
Let's drink!

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.590
I'm here!

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:27.670
Everyone from Tsukinoki is here, too!

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.670
<i>Where did they come from?</i>

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:32.620
<i>Thinking about it is a waste of time.</i>

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:35.030
Okay, we're here.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:47.230
<i>Are they human?</i>

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.190
How wonderful.

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:56.320
This looks so good.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:58.380
Thank you for the invitation.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.760
Oh, it's Doctor Fujiyuki...

00:15:01.760 --> 00:15:03.030
Been a while.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:05.160
Good to see you haven't changed, Isshiki-san.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:09.340
<i>Doctor Fujiyuki... Akine-chan's master!</i>

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:13.870
<i>He's supposed to be a spiritualist, 
but he sure looks like a doctor.</i>

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:17.860
Yushi-kun, this is Doctor Fujiyuki.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:18.890
Hello.

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:21.530
I'm Yushi Inaba.

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.280
Nice to meet you!

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.480
Is he the bearer of the magic book?

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:31.350
Yushi-kun is working really hard.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.530
He's cute.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:36.460
<i>I'm being treated like a kid.</i>

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:40.800
<i>Does he cast spells and control familiars?</i>

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:44.450
You can't judge a book by its cover, huh?

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.460
All right, let's get started!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.390
Cheers!

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:04.620
Fool...

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:06.970
Seems things are getting lively.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:08.960
It's a moon-viewing party.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.400
That is wonderful!

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:15.660
The moon has always been 
intimately related to magic.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:16.950
Mm-hmm.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:19.550
Especially the full moon, 
which enhances spiritual power.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:24.140
So tonight, please bathe in 
the moonlight, master.

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:29.990
Increasing your spiritual power 
increases ours, as well!

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:31.090
Mm-hmm.

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:33.620
That's right!

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:37.230
I shouldn't have worked so 
hard to pound the mochi.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:41.130
I could have had the omnipotent 
spirit Jin do it!

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:43.850
Well, that is true,

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:46.970
but I don't know if that is how a 
mage should use his summons.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:50.900
What's wrong?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.370
The moon's so pretty.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.810
How can you be so sad?

00:16:55.810 --> 00:16:57.500
Drink! Drink!

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:59.900
Don't let stuff bug you! Let's drink!

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.830
The master is underage!

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.240
Then, we'll go take a bath.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:06.600
A bath!

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:08.630
N-No more baths!

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:12.660
This is wonderful.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:14.960
It's good. So good.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:18.080
Are these your only patients?

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:18.880
No.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:22.600
Some patients can't come, of course.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:27.560
So they're doing the same thing 
in the hospital courtyard.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.630
Right, Masa-san?

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:32.980
I'm lucky I got to come here!

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:36.590
I didn't think the sake would be so good.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:39.900
<i>Is he a psychic, too?</i>

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.670
Masa-san, your true identity's showing.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:45.530
It's showing.

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:46.510
Oops.

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:49.410
<i>He wasn't human...</i>

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:50.850
I want mochi, too, chirp.

00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:52.280
Sticky mochi, chirp.

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:54.870
It's so sticky!

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:56.850
Yay! Chirp!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.740
Kuri, what are you doing?

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:29.640
How many dumplings did 
you have? You'll get sick.

00:18:29.640 --> 00:18:31.160
Your child?

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.080
No!

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:36.510
He's so cute.

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:41.350
Are you okay?

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:46.370
I was just remembering the past.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.280
If I'd had even one cute kid like this,

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:54.520
I'm sure my life would have been different.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:05.200
You'll let me hold you? That's so nice.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.390
Look, Yushi.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:12.880
Did you know that bunnies live on the moon?

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:15.880
They make mochi!

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:18.130
Grandma...

00:19:18.490 --> 00:19:21.670
It was a painful, pathetic life.

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:27.090
But in the end, I was able to feel great.

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:31.520
And even a wonderful moon-viewing party.

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:34.650
Thank you.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:37.780
Not at all...

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:42.370
Thank you all, as well.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:47.570
Someday, when I die, I'll be happy.

00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:51.630
That's how I feel now, thanks to you.

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:55.040
Now I can go to heaven.

00:19:57.530 --> 00:20:00.690
Thank you all, doctors.

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:03.340
Let's meet again somewhere.

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.550
Goodbye.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.860
Thank you.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:21.200
Oh, my... Hatsu-san's so quick to leave us.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:22.710
Shall we go...

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:24.300
...as well?

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:27.460
You're leaving?

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:29.110
Thank you for everything.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:31.380
Go and be reborn.

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:35.820
Next time, I hope life is a little easier.

00:20:51.780 --> 00:20:53.550
<i>So she was a ghost.</i>

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:55.990
Those people died today.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:01.240
I'm glad we were able to give them 
good memories before the end!

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:03.580
That's our job.

00:21:05.330 --> 00:21:08.510
Is heaven really above the sky?

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:11.890
If you think it is, then it is.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:15.380
Just as the moon's spiritual energy 
takes the form of a rabbit.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:17.600
I see.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:23.200
<i>They must've felt like
they could go to heaven.</i>

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:26.570
<i>I'm glad.</i>

00:23:11.130 --> 00:23:13.490
Heaven's above the sky, right?

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:14.740
Then, where's hell?

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:16.620
It's everywhere.

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:17.530
Furuhonya-san?

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:21.160
How much hell have I seen around the world?

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:23.430
Tonight, you'll find out all about it.

00:23:23.430 --> 00:23:24.720
You won't be getting any sleep.

00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:27.220
There's hell right here.

00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:30.720
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:33.330
The Road to Hell Is Paved 
With Good Intentions.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:33.760
<b>Seventeenth Haunting 
The Road to Hell Is Paved With Good Intentions</b>

00:23:33.750 --> 00:23:35.860
Is Aoki-sensei's kindness...
